<title>USA: Safety 1st Q4 shr loss $5.33 with charge.</title>
<headline>Safety 1st Q4 shr loss $5.33 with charge.</headline>
<dateline>CHESTNUT HILL, Mass. 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Safety 1st Inc (in thousands, except per share)</p>
<p>			    Fourth Quarter Ended     Year Ended</p>
<p>			     12/31/96  12/31/95  12/31/96 12/31/95</p>
<p>Net sales		   $15,910   $22,330  $105,752 $103,218</p>
<p>Cost of sales		24,683    17,668    86,672   68,673</p>
<p>S, G &amp; A expenses	  22,080     8,481    56,692   28,320</p>
<p>Impairment of l-l assets 10,226	  --    11,596	 --</p>
<p>Operating income (loss) (41,079)   (3,819)  (49,208)   6,225</p>
<p>Interest expense</p>
<p>   (income), net	    1,775	 366     4,100    1,066</p>
<p>Net income (loss)	$(38,127)  $(2,501) $(44,849)  $3,200</p>
<p>Net income(loss) per shr $(5.33)   $(0.35)   $(6.27)   $0.45</p>
<p>Avg shrs outstanding	7,156     7,132     7,157    7,132</p>
<p>NOTE: Safety 1st recorded a $32.7 million pretax charge in the fourth quarter associated with a redefining of its business strategy, particularly the previously announced realignment of the Safety 1st product mix, including a $10.2 million charge in connection with SFAS 121.</p>
<p>Excluding the pretax charges, the company would have recorded a fourth quarter pretax loss of $10.1 million.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1700</p>
